## 7. Editor ↔ server protocol

```
server → client  { type: "scene", scene, history: { canUndo, canRedo, undoLabel?, redoLabel? } }
server → client  { type: "created", requestId, ids }      // reply to add_boxes, so the editor can select the new box
server → client  { type: "error", message }

client → server  { type: "add_boxes", requestId, boxes: [{ kind, x, z, width, depth, height? }] }
client → server  { type: "update_boxes", changes: [{ id, height }] }
client → server  { type: "undo" } | { type: "redo" } | { type: "clear" }
client → server  { type: "set_view", view }
```

The full scene is still sent on every change, and the client still renders whatever the server says. The only new thing is the `created` reply, because auto-selecting a freshly drawn box needs its server-assigned ID.

